# Release & Versioning

## Which repository

| Work | Tags / Releases live on |
|------|-------------------------|
| Code under `projects/<name>/` | That sub-project's GitHub repo |
| Template at workspace root | This template repo |

Tag the **default branch** commit after merge (usually `main`). Do not tag feature branches.

## Version format (SemVer)

- GitHub tag / Release: `v{MAJOR}.{MINOR}.{PATCH}` (e.g. `v1.4.2`)
- Manifests (`package.json`, etc.): same numbers **without** `v` (e.g. `1.4.2`)
- Standard: [semver.org](https://semver.org)

## Bump rules (from Conventional Commits)

| Bump | Triggers | Example |
|------|----------|---------|
| PATCH | `fix`, `chore(deps)`, `docs`, `style` | `v0.7.1` → `v0.7.2` |
| MINOR | `feat`, `refactor` (API unchanged) | `v0.7.0` → `v0.8.0` (PATCH → 0) |
| MAJOR | `type(scope)!` or `BREAKING CHANGE` footer | `v0.7.0` → `v1.0.0` (MINOR/PATCH → 0) |

### `0.x.x` (initial development)

- Breaking change → **MINOR +1**, not MAJOR (until `1.0.0`).
- Promote to `1.0.0` when: core features stable, docs/tests in place, public API unlikely to churn (sub-project may document criteria in ADR).

### Pre-release

`v1.0.0-alpha.1`, `v1.0.0-beta.1`, `v1.0.0-rc.1` — internal / external / RC only; final drop the suffix.

## Tag naming

| OK | Not OK |
|----|--------|
| `v1.4.2` | `V1.4.2`, `version-1.4.2`, `release-1.4.2` |

Published tags are **immutable** — do not retag or force-move.

## Release notes

Group squash-merged commits (PR title = squash message) by type. Headings: Features, Bug Fixes, Breaking Changes, Chores. Optional automation: `release-please`, `semantic-release`.

## When to tag

Tag when: deployable milestone, hotfix, sprint end. **Do not** tag every commit or every PR merge.

## AI behavior

| Action | Policy |
|--------|--------|
| Suggest next version / draft release notes | Allowed from commits since last tag |
| Create git tag or GitHub Release | **Explicit user request only** |
| Edit published release notes | Explicit request only |
| Delete or move published tag | **Forbidden** |

See skill `release-workflow`. Sub-projects may override in `projects/<name>/.cursor/rules/`. Major versioning policy changes → ADR under `docs/adr/`.
